<given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Seyfer</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reconstructive surgery: lower extremity coverage</article-title><source>Mathes Plastic Surgery</source><year>2006</year><edition>2nd ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia, PA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Elsevier</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wheeless</surname><given-names>CR</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Soft tissue coverage for the leg</article-title><source>Wheeless' Textbook of Orthopaedics</source><year>2011</year><publisher-name>Data Trace Internet Publishing, LLC</publisher-name><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.wheelessonline.com">http://www.wheelessonline.com</ext-link>. Acessed March 31, 2012</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Attinger</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Ducic</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Thorne</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartlett</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Beasley</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Aston</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gurtner</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Spear</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Foot and ankle reconstruction</article-title><source>Grabb and Smith's Plastic Surgery</source><year>2007</year><edition>6th ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia, PA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lippincott Williams &#x00026; Wilkins</publisher-name><fpage>689</fpage><lpage>707</lpage></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Lower extremity defect status post serial debridement. Exposed hardware can be seen.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty13ic31_fig1"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Lateral gastrocnemius muscle flap.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty13ic31_fig2"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Postoperative result at 1 month showing split-thickness skin graft.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty13ic31_fig3"/></fig></floats-group></article>